                <pb facs="0735" n="665" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg665"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. Romero to Mr
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexican Legation in the United States of
                                America, Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-08-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 26, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Romero’s respects to Mr. Seward, and has the honor to send him a copy of a
                    communication from General Berriozabal, commander on the Rio Grande, dated the
                    9th instant, in Matamoros, and annexed documents, in one of which Mr. Manuel Z.
                    Gomez, governor of the State of New Leon, denies the authenticity of a letter
                    attributed to General Escobedo, in which he gives utterance to remarks against
                    foreigners residing in Mexico.</p>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>





